    "required_height": 0.6555555555555554
  },
  {
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 0.75,
    "y": 17.29138888888889,
    "w": 11.0,
    "h": 2.163333333333333,
    "text": "In-situ ground truth for soil moisture comes from NOAA USCRN and SNOTEL stations. Satellite inputs comprise SMAP soil moisture, Sentinel-1 radar backscatter from the land surface, and Sentinel-2 surface reflectance and indices of vegetation greenness and canopy water content. We use MODIS land-surface temperature, ERA5-Land weather, and terrain, soil, and climate descriptors.",
    "lines": [
      "In-situ ground truth for soil moisture comes from NOAA USCRN and",
      "SNOTEL stations. Satellite inputs comprise SMAP soil moisture,",
      "Sentinel-1 radar backscatter from the land surface, and Sentinel-2",
      "surface reflectance and indices of vegetation greenness and canopy",
      "water content. We use MODIS land-surface temperature, ERA5-Land",
      "weather, and terrain, soil, and climate descriptors."
    ],
    "size": 22,
    "color": "#202B35",
    "bold": false,
    "align": "left",
    "name": "",
    "required_height": 2.163333333333333
  },
  {
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 0.75,
    "y": 19.57472222222222,
    "w": 11.0,
    "h": 1.0816666666666666,
    "text": "The data pipeline aligns observations onto a daily grid, imputes missing values, smooths temporal sequences, and extracts rolling lag features capturing recent weather and satellite signals.",
    "lines": [
      "The data pipeline aligns observations onto a daily grid, imputes",
      "missing values, smooths temporal sequences, and extracts rolling lag",
      "features capturing recent weather and satellite signals."
    ],
    "size": 22,
