  {
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 12.5,
    "y": 12.232222222222223,
    "w": 11.0,
    "h": 0.6555555555555554,
    "text": "Figure 2. Two-regime routing: each observation is assigned to a specialist f\u1d63, where x denotes input features, s the station, and g the routing function.",
    "lines": [
      "Figure 2. Two-regime routing: each observation is assigned to a specialist f\u1d63,",
      "where x denotes input features, s the station, and g the routing function."
    ],
    "size": 20,
    "color": "#536875",
    "bold": false,
    "align": "left",
    "name": "",
    "required_height": 0.6555555555555554
  },
  {
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 12.5,
    "y": 13.007777777777779,
    "w": 11.0,
    "h": 1.442222222222222,
    "text": "1. Router inputs are imputed using training-set means and standardized to comparable scales. K-means clustering identifies two centroids, assigning unseen samples to the nearest centroid using feature inputs alone without target labels.",
    "lines": [
      "1. Router inputs are imputed using training-set means and",
      "standardized to comparable scales. K-means clustering identifies two",
      "centroids, assigning unseen samples to the nearest centroid using",
      "feature inputs alone without target labels."
    ],
    "size": 22,
    "color": "#202B35",
    "bold": false,
    "align": "left",
    "name": "",
    "required_height": 1.442222222222222
  },
  {
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 12.5,
    "y": 14.57,
    "w": 11.0,
    "h": 1.0816666666666666,
    "text": "2. For known stations, each adopts its majority cluster specialist for temporal consistency. New stations are routed dynamically each day, falling back to rainfall rules if satellite features are missing.",
    "lines": [
      "2. For known stations, each adopts its majority cluster specialist for",
      "temporal consistency. New stations are routed dynamically each day,",
      "falling back to rainfall rules if satellite features are missing."
    ],
    "size": 22,
    "color": "#202B35",
    "bold": false,
    "align": "left",
    "name": "",
    "required_height": 1.0816666666666666
  },
  {
    "kind": "text",
    "x": 12.5,
    "y": 15.771666666666667,
    "w": 11.0,
    "h": 1.8027777777777776,
    "text": "3. Both approaches use identical features, XGBoost settings, evaluation splits, and random seeds. Each specialist trains solely on its assigned regime. Testing 30 repeated seeds quantifies training stability, while station-holdout splits evaluate spatial generalization uncertainty.",
    "lines": [
      "3. Both approaches use identical features, XGBoost settings,",
